! Similar to Prime groups, except you're asked to return a count of all of
! the unique prime groupings of the input string.
! 
! -   A prime grouping is a grouping of n characters from a string, where
!     all pairs of its absolute differences between the characters'
!     character codes are primes.
! 
! Here, a is defined as the largest number through which a prime group
! with n characters may be found.
! 
! Specifically:
! 
! -   Input a string from the user.
! -   Print a number:
!     -   the count of all prime groupings in that string, from 2 to a.


